<title>FINLAND: NOKIA, ERICSSON WIN ORDERS FROM TELIA'S TELIVO.</title>
<headline>NOKIA, ERICSSON WIN ORDERS FROM TELIA'S TELIVO.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telivo, the Finnish unit of Swedish tele operator Telia, said on Wednesday Finnish Nokia would supply it with a DCS 1800 cellular phone network and Swedish Ericsson with an ATM data network.</p>
<p>It did not give the value of orders.</p>
<p>&quot;Construction of the DCS 1800 network network has begun and at the turn of the year, it will cover the largest cities in Finland,&quot; Telivo said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Telivo said it expected to launch data transfer services at the end of the year.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
